(1309441, 160808, 23394, '<td valign="top">excellent capture!  i''m really struggling with my new 50mm lens now, trying to get just a step beyond this.  this is hard enough, but i want to get this type of shot absolutely razor sharp, with very little softness--you know, so the catchlights are large and distinct.  i''ve had a bit better luck shooting at iso400, and i haven''t been experiencing that much noise, either.  the other thing i''ve found useful is to pick a single af point and use it without recomposing.  all i can say is ''thank God for digital'', because i sure couldn''t afford to do all the practice it takes to nail a shot like this if i was paying for film...<br/> <br/>oh well, enough about me...wonderful image, good luck!</td>', 'excellent capture!  i''m really struggling with my new 50mm lens now, trying to get just a step beyond this.  this is hard enough, but i want to get this type of shot absolutely razor sharp, with very little softness--you know, so the catchlights are large and distinct.  i''ve had a bit better luck shooting at iso400, and i haven''t been experiencing that much noise, either.  the other thing i''ve found useful is to pick a single af point and use it without recomposing.  all i can say is ''thank God for digital'', because i sure couldn''t afford to do all the practice it takes to nail a shot like this if i was paying for film... oh well, enough about me...wonderful image, good luck!', '2005-04-20 21:52:03.000000', NULL, 1),
