(1318006, 164877, 6999, '<td valign="top">You could darken this enormously, i think: in the sense that there are no blown-out highlights it isn''t over-exposed of course; but in the sense that all the colours lack vibrancy, and a sense of contrast throughout the image, then it <i>is</i> over-exposed. Cameras meter in an odd way, and it''s almost always worth shooting with the exposure compensation set down a stop or two: darker images can always be brought up in processing.<br/> <br/>I think this scene is a bit complex to work well as a reflection: certainly at the submission size here. The figures, the dome, the flowers, the house, the greenery ... and the over-lapping of many of those leaves you with an image where there is too much stuff going on for the reflection to stand out.</td>', 'You could darken this enormously, i think: in the sense that there are no blown-out highlights it isn''t over-exposed of course; but in the sense that all the colours lack vibrancy, and a sense of contrast throughout the image, then it is over-exposed. Cameras meter in an odd way, and it''s almost always worth shooting with the exposure compensation set down a stop or two: darker images can always be brought up in processing. I think this scene is a bit complex to work well as a reflection: certainly at the submission size here. The figures, the dome, the flowers, the house, the greenery ... and the over-lapping of many of those leaves you with an image where there is too much stuff going on for the reflection to stand out.', '2005-04-24 11:13:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1318008, 165581, 12909, '<td valign="top">Very cute photo. nice use of depth of field</td>', 'Very cute photo. nice use of depth of field', '2005-04-24 11:14:05.000000', NULL, 1),
