(1325700, 168303, 23394, '<td valign="top">this looks like a vista that has potential, but for this image, it''s a bit too soft.  the composition is ok, but i can''t get enough of a feel for your primary subject to really be taken in by it.  if that''s water down below, though, you might want to scout around for some places to shoot the reflections...</td>', 'this looks like a vista that has potential, but for this image, it''s a bit too soft.  the composition is ok, but i can''t get enough of a feel for your primary subject to really be taken in by it.  if that''s water down below, though, you might want to scout around for some places to shoot the reflections...', '2005-04-25 20:31:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1325703, 166767, 5792, '<td valign="top">Image appears to be over processed for colors. Colors seem unrealstic. Oversharpening or separate processing between sky and horizon resulted in distracting haloing. Might have considered offsetting the moon to one side or the other of the frame as opposed to having it directly in the middle.</td>', 'Image appears to be over processed for colors. Colors seem unrealstic. Oversharpening or separate processing between sky and horizon resulted in distracting haloing. Might have considered offsetting the moon to one side or the other of the frame as opposed to having it directly in the middle.', '2005-04-25 20:33:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1325707, 162733, 23394, '<td valign="top">interesting image.  you might consider a shadow/highlight adjustment, though, to bring out some of the detail on the animal.  as is, it''s just too much in the shadows to really appreciate.  you might also consider a less centered composition the next time you happen upon one of these beasts.  it''s one thing if you want to shoot a straight documentary shot, it''s another thing if you want to create an engaging image the captivates and keeps the viewer for awhile.  hope this does well for you.  good luck!</td>', 'interesting image.  you might consider a shadow/highlight adjustment, though, to bring out some of the detail on the animal.  as is, it''s just too much in the shadows to really appreciate.  you might also consider a less centered composition the next time you happen upon one of these beasts.  it''s one thing if you want to shoot a straight documentary shot, it''s another thing if you want to create an engaging image the captivates and keeps the viewer for awhile.  hope this does well for you.  good luck!', '2005-04-25 20:33:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1325709, 167444, 28108, '<td valign="top">This beautifull picture would have more impact if the right and bottom thirds were cropped out.</td>', 'This beautifull picture would have more impact if the right and bottom thirds were cropped out.', '2005-04-25 20:34:09.000000', NULL, 1),
