(1327767, 165688, 35357, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the great comments.  I''m going to dig up the original &amp; see why I didn''t crop further to the left, which is such good advice I don''t understand why I didn''t do it, there must have been a llama standing in the way or something, hopefully not.<br/> <br/>The water there is naturally very yellow, I don''t know why.  I''m going to see if I can paint some desaturation over it to make it white.<br/> <br/>If things turn out, I might actually print it out and stick it on my wall.<br/> <br/>I would''ve liked to have done a longer exposure to soften the water, alas it was very sunny out (hence the rainbow), I don''t have a filter for my little point &amp; shoot, and I left my sunglasses back in my car, so I couldn''t even use them. :-(<br/> <br/>:-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-04-26 08:29:51.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all the great comments.  I''m going to dig up the original & see why I didn''t crop further to the left, which is such good advice I don''t understand why I didn''t do it, there must have been a llama standing in the way or something, hopefully not. The water there is naturally very yellow, I don''t know why.  I''m going to see if I can paint some desaturation over it to make it white. If things turn out, I might actually print it out and stick it on my wall. I would''ve liked to have done a longer exposure to soften the water, alas it was very sunny out (hence the rainbow), I don''t have a filter for my little point & shoot, and I left my sunglasses back in my car, so I couldn''t even use them. :-( :-)', '2005-04-26 09:27:20.000000', '2005-04-26 09:29:51.000000', 0),
