 + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//nordic1966.100webcustomers.com/Follies/thumbnails/tynedale_5.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Thanks,<br/>Neil<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-05-11 16:31:32.</i></td>', 'Thanks to everybody who took the time to comment. Some of the other images I took that evening:   Thanks,Neil', '2005-04-26 15:17:46.000000', '2005-05-11 17:31:32.000000', 0),
(1328839, 168336, 1845, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mk:</b></div><hr/><i> Was the experiment a success or a failure? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I presume you mean the entering of the photo in the challenge was the experiment.  It was not.  Although there is always the stray chance of the inexplicable happening, this shot was destined for brown.  The photo itself was an experiment.<br/> <br/>Interestingly, the shot doesn''t meet any of charliebaker''s <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=171805" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">How to Win the Brown Ribbon</a>, except perhaps 2, although the focus is necessarily the way it is.<br/> <br/>The shot was not taken to get the brown and it is among my favourites for the challenge period.</td>', 'Originally posted by mk: Was the experiment a success or a failure?  I presume you mean the entering of the photo in the challenge was the experiment.  It was not.  Although there is always the stray chance of the inexplicable happening, this shot was destined for brown.  The photo itself was an experiment. Interestingly, the shot doesn''t meet any of charliebaker''s How to Win the Brown Ribbon, except perhaps 2, although the focus is necessarily the way it is. The shot was not taken to get the brown and it is among my favourites for the challenge period.', '2005-04-26 15:25:09.000000', NULL, 0),
