(1330914, 161133, 19708, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by samtrundle:</b></div><hr/><i>Though I have to say, there''s no way I could have done mine without a tripod - them''s some ridiculously sturdy hands you''ve got yourself.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>It also helps to NOT have a mirror to slap around inside the camera! <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by samtrundle:</b></div><hr/><i>As for the photo itself, I really like the warm feel and the diffused effect your processing gives it (or was that just camera shake induced blur :P). </i></td></tr></table> <br/>:P Back! LOL</td>', 'Originally posted by samtrundle:Though I have to say, there''s no way I could have done mine without a tripod - them''s some ridiculously sturdy hands you''ve got yourself. It also helps to NOT have a mirror to slap around inside the camera!  Originally posted by samtrundle:As for the photo itself, I really like the warm feel and the diffused effect your processing gives it (or was that just camera shake induced blur :P).  :P Back! LOL', '2005-04-27 03:50:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1331067, 167305, 23394, '<td valign="top">for cloning something like this, it does take a bit of work.  you need to be zoomed it pretty deep, and you''ll also need to go back and forth between the clone stamp and the healing brush.  work with it when you have time--this would be a great image to practice on, AND you''d wind up with a killer print!  have fun!</td>', 'for cloning something like this, it does take a bit of work.  you need to be zoomed it pretty deep, and you''ll also need to go back and forth between the clone stamp and the healing brush.  work with it when you have time--this would be a great image to practice on, AND you''d wind up with a killer print!  have fun!', '2005-04-27 04:37:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(1331090, 162436, 23394, '<td valign="top">wow, neil, you must have had a dickens of a time deciding which to enter--they are all outstanding!  i like the first one for the additional interest in the clouds, but really love the 4th one!  excellent diagonals and colors.</td>', 'wow, neil, you must have had a dickens of a time deciding which to enter--they are all outstanding!  i like the first one for the additional interest in the clouds, but really love the 4th one!  excellent diagonals and colors.', '2005-04-27 05:09:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1331650, 167124, 20204, '<td valign="top">This is one of the few times I didn''t make it to 100% of the images...  Obviously I''m being punished for that.   Lately I''ve really been appreciating simple compositions, and this is one of them.  This image is so clean and crisp I can almost smell a faint residue of wine while viewing it.  Not sure why it didn''t place higher - this is outstanding work as always.</td>', 'This is one of the few times I didn''t make it to 100% of the images...  Obviously I''m being punished for that.   Lately I''ve really been appreciating simple compositions, and this is one of them.  This image is so clean and crisp I can almost smell a faint residue of wine while viewing it.  Not sure why it didn''t place higher - this is outstanding work as always.', '2005-04-27 09:25:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1331666, 168333, 20204, '<td valign="top">Keep pursuing this path - you''ve show a very unique style with this one that I would love to see more of.  Maybe a few refinements could be made, but I believe that this image''s composition and concet stand above minor technical flaws.  Great work!</td>', 'Keep pursuing this path - you''ve show a very unique style with this one that I would love to see more of.  Maybe a few refinements could be made, but I believe that this image''s composition and concet stand above minor technical flaws.  Great work!', '2005-04-27 09:29:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(1332261, 163575, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment: </b> <br/> <br/>First of all, I want to say that I have myself tried night photography and I am not the best at it.<br/>It''s hard to get exposure right, there are so many things to take in account when trying, it''s not my favorite kind of photography to do, but the results can be great.<br/> <br/>I have voted on all entries in the free study and voted this a 6.<br/>I can tell you why, now that I have looked at your image longer I understand what you where trying to say, but when voting on 500+ photos people dont take the time to look really hard.<br/> <br/>I don''t know for sure if I would have voted higher if I understood it right away, maybe a point more.<br/>The trouble with this picture is there''s so much going on, the fence, the light on the fence the light in the doorway, that it is not easy to find a place of interest. And that way your message doesnt come across.<br/>Also keep in mind that people send in their best shots (well most of the time) and there will be some great ones in every free study. Because of the high number of really great photos the average goes down, so dont be disappointed with your score, its tough to compete with so many great photos<br/> <br/>I think Frisca''s comment says it all, without the fence this would have been much better.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work. <br/> <br/>Peter <br/> <br/>If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me. <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-04-27 10:20:15.</i></td>', 'Critique Club Comment:   First of all, I want to say that I have myself tried night photography and I am not the best at it.It''s hard to get exposure right, there are so many things to take in account when trying, it''s not my favorite kind of photography to do, but the results can be great. I have voted on all entries in the free study and voted this a 6.I can tell you why, now that I have looked at your image longer I understand what you where trying to say, but when voting on 500+ photos people dont take the time to look really hard. I don''t know for sure if I would have voted higher if I understood it right away, maybe a point more.The trouble with this picture is there''s so much going on, the fence, the light on the fence the light in the doorway, that it is not easy to find a place of interest. And that way your message doesnt come across.Also keep in mind that people send in their best shots (well most of the time) and there will be some great ones in every free study. Because of the high number of really great photos the average goes down, so dont be disappointed with your score, its tough to compete with so many great photos I think Frisca''s comment says it all, without the fence this would have been much better. Keep up the good work.  Peter  If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me. ', '2005-04-27 11:19:17.000000', '2005-04-27 11:20:15.000000', 0),
