(1370867, 168336, 9668, '<td valign="top">The steps of How to Win the Brown Ribbon is guidelines, not rules for doing it. If you followed all thet steps, you''d be high in the running for a brown.<br/> <br/>According to your photo I think that:<br/>STEP ONE: Do not fit your photo to the challenge. <br/>- Think that is kindof impossible to do in a free study.<br/>STEP TWO: Take a low quality photo in camera. <br/>- I think the blur and tilt meets this<br/>STEP THREE: Over-edit to enhance the low quality of the photo.<br/>- Nope, I don''t think you edited it.<br/>STEP FOUR: Use an obscure, overly-long, misspeled or redundant title.<br/>- Nope, title is normal<br/>STEP FIVE: Laugh out loud.<br/>- Hope you did =)<br/> <br/>It is interesting to get a brown with only meeting one section of the "criteria" (although I hope you met the Laugh out loud part &lt;smile&gt;). A free study is a premium place fo this: people expect high quality images and it is impossible not to meet the challenge. I like your idea experimental photography though; it may be ludicrous, but so was Picasso''s idea of cubism when he first started.</td>', 'The steps of How to Win the Brown Ribbon is guidelines, not rules for doing it. If you followed all thet steps, you''d be high in the running for a brown. According to your photo I think that:STEP ONE: Do not fit your photo to the challenge. - Think that is kindof impossible to do in a free study.STEP TWO: Take a low quality photo in camera. - I think the blur and tilt meets thisSTEP THREE: Over-edit to enhance the low quality of the photo.- Nope, I don''t think you edited it.STEP FOUR: Use an obscure, overly-long, misspeled or redundant title.- Nope, title is normalSTEP FIVE: Laugh out loud.- Hope you did =) It is interesting to get a brown with only meeting one section of the "criteria" (although I hope you met the Laugh out loud part <smile>). A free study is a premium place fo this: people expect high quality images and it is impossible not to meet the challenge. I like your idea experimental photography though; it may be ludicrous, but so was Picasso''s idea of cubism when he first started.', '2005-05-08 06:34:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1372457, 167124, 9906, '<td valign="top">Setz, every once in a while, I see shots that break so many rules but still work as a total composition.  This is one of them.  There is SO MUCH going on in this shot that at first the eye is confused and doesn''t know where to end up.  But with the simple tonality and the simple lines it really doesn''t matter too much.  Wherever the eye lands there is a new detail for it to take in!  I do find myself ending up on the dark cork, but that''s OK cause with the lines leading away from it, I just start the journey all over again!<br/>TC</td>', 'Setz, every once in a while, I see shots that break so many rules but still work as a total composition.  This is one of them.  There is SO MUCH going on in this shot that at first the eye is confused and doesn''t know where to end up.  But with the simple tonality and the simple lines it really doesn''t matter too much.  Wherever the eye lands there is a new detail for it to take in!  I do find myself ending up on the dark cork, but that''s OK cause with the lines leading away from it, I just start the journey all over again!TC', '2005-05-09 02:16:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1373070, 164671, 8860, '<td valign="top">What do you mean "a big thank you to Scott"? He''s the one who should be thanking you!<br/>; )</td>', 'What do you mean "a big thank you to Scott"? He''s the one who should be thanking you!; )', '2005-05-09 11:25:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1374742, 166050, 22207, '<td valign="top">This cat reminds me of my lovely old cat that died 10 years ago.  You can see the character shining out of Smokey''s eyes.  Does she have any available offspring?</td>', 'This cat reminds me of my lovely old cat that died 10 years ago.  You can see the character shining out of Smokey''s eyes.  Does she have any available offspring?', '2005-05-10 04:39:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1375008, 166567, 8860, '<td valign="top">No problem Digitalknight - the original is <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=176281" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a> for anyone who is interested in seeing the out-of-camera shot. <br/> <br/>I could have used fill-flash for subject like this, but it would have destroyed the subtlety of the light. On checking the histogram I knew that I had all the data I needed, but it just needed to be brought out with some help in post-processing.</td>', 'No problem Digitalknight - the original is here for anyone who is interested in seeing the out-of-camera shot.  I could have used fill-flash for subject like this, but it would have destroyed the subtlety of the light. On checking the histogram I knew that I had all the data I needed, but it just needed to be brought out with some help in post-processing.', '2005-05-10 09:27:06.000000', NULL, 0),
