(1933366, 167350, 43671, '<td valign="top">James, thank you for letting me write it. I really like the pic. Jeff</td>', 'James, thank you for letting me write it. I really like the pic. Jeff', '2005-12-07 19:28:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1934312, 161112, 39057, '<td valign="top">I bet this girl would kill for a copy of this shot!</td>', 'I bet this girl would kill for a copy of this shot!', '2005-12-07 23:49:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1936674, 167289, 30861, '<td valign="top">As far as overall tonalities go, this is an exceptionally lovely image. Pgatt, you''re getting VERY good at B/W conversions. Since you''ve asked me to comment upon the image, I have these observations:<br/> <br/>1. The composition is pretty static, and that hurts it. It divides more or less equally into an upper and lower zone, with the two pretty much in stasis. If, for example, the pier were longer and thrusting further into the "upper zone" that would be more dynamic. Additionally, the foreground piling is seriously orphaned and OOF to boot, which isn''t good.<br/> <br/>2. The lower left of the image is blocked to black; it seems to have been burned in (I can''t be sure) and it really wants a trace more detail brought up, especially where the piling is reflecting and also in the "construction details" between the pilings.<br/> <br/>I can imagine that if this were extended on the left to make a "normally proportioned" rectangle, that alone would strengthen the composition quite a bit. I''d like to see the original on this.<br/> <br/>Good work!</td>', 'As far as overall tonalities go, this is an exceptionally lovely image. Pgatt, you''re getting VERY good at B/W conversions. Since you''ve asked me to comment upon the image, I have these observations: 1. The composition is pretty static, and that hurts it. It divides more or less equally into an upper and lower zone, with the two pretty much in stasis. If, for example, the pier were longer and thrusting further into the "upper zone" that would be more dynamic. Additionally, the foreground piling is seriously orphaned and OOF to boot, which isn''t good. 2. The lower left of the image is blocked to black; it seems to have been burned in (I can''t be sure) and it really wants a trace more detail brought up, especially where the piling is reflecting and also in the "construction details" between the pilings. I can imagine that if this were extended on the left to make a "normally proportioned" rectangle, that alone would strengthen the composition quite a bit. I''d like to see the original on this. Good work!', '2005-12-08 22:18:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1953910, 161133, 23394, '<td valign="top">splendid work, brad.  i somehow missed this before, glad i found it now.</td>', 'splendid work, brad.  i somehow missed this before, glad i found it now.', '2005-12-15 12:23:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1974262, 167500, 34659, '<td valign="top">Amazing clarity and DOF - simply beautiful.  I really like the composition too - the negative space works well.  I must admit I think I scored this too low (6) in the challenge - it definitely deserved 8+.  Very nice piece of work.</td>', 'Amazing clarity and DOF - simply beautiful.  I really like the composition too - the negative space works well.  I must admit I think I scored this too low (6) in the challenge - it definitely deserved 8+.  Very nice piece of work.', '2005-12-23 16:12:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978098, 168169, 14212, '<td valign="top">Sure wish you had a print ready!</td>', 'Sure wish you had a print ready!', '2005-12-26 02:51:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(1988939, 164586, 30364, '<td valign="top">I must have been sleeping all last April to have missed this brilliant photograph.  I''ve just looked; the three ribbon winners in that challenge were all terrific images, but I would have voted this one ahead even of those.  It''s a beautiful work.</td>', 'I must have been sleeping all last April to have missed this brilliant photograph.  I''ve just looked; the three ribbon winners in that challenge were all terrific images, but I would have voted this one ahead even of those.  It''s a beautiful work.', '2005-12-30 17:43:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2031677, 168169, 28359, '<td valign="top">I knew this tree farm would be a great shot. I drive by it at least once or twice a year going to Spokane or Boise. You did a great job. I don''t think I''ve seen them this bright and colorful. Once again, nice work...........ace</td>', 'I knew this tree farm would be a great shot. I drive by it at least once or twice a year going to Spokane or Boise. You did a great job. I don''t think I''ve seen them this bright and colorful. Once again, nice work...........ace', '2006-01-12 23:19:10.000000', NULL, 0),
